    "result_text": "The build passes. Here's a summary of what I implemented.\n\n## Change: `customerCode` assignment\n\nThe spec required assigning each new owner a `customerCode` formatted `<LAST3>-<NNNN>` \u2014 upper-cased first three letters of the last name, plus a global 4-digit zero-padded sequence equal to one more than the current owner count.\n\n**Files changed:**\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `customerCode` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` (returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`) exposes it. MapStruct maps it automatically by matching name.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added the persisted `customerCode` field (`@Column(name = \"customer_code\")`) with getter/setter, following the existing entity idiom.\n\n3. **`src/main/java/.../rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, assign `owner.setCustomerCode(nextCustomerCode(owner.getLastName()))` before saving. The new `nextCustomerCode` helper computes `LAST3` (`substring(0, min(3, len)).toUpperCase()`) and the sequence as `findAllOwners().size() + 1`, formatted with `%s-%04d`. It's set only on create, not on update.\n\n4. **DB schemas** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `customer_code` column to the `owners` table. Tests run on hsqldb; the others were updated for consistency.\n\n**Verification:** The `AcceptanceTest.coreFormatAndGlobalSequence` test passes \u2014 `smithers` \u2192 `SMI-####`, `jones` \u2192 `JON-####`, with consecutive sequence numbers. Full suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test run, 0 failures.",
